# Shell scripts run on the Ubuntu server and must keep LF endings.
#
# `competitor_visual_pass.sh` reached the server with CRLF on
# 2026-11-03 — the day `scripts/provision` was first included in
# the deploy — and bash answered:
#
#   set: pipefail: invalid option name
#   syntax error near unexpected token `$'{\r''
#
# which the owner saw as "Did not finish, exited with code 2".
# A carriage return is invisible in every editor and in every
# diff, so this is enforced here rather than remembered.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reason: these are read by the server, not by Windows.
*.py text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
